A||||25||qwikgta||Lets have some FUN....Who has the most interesting FACT about the Fiero||||1||
Z||000000||qwikgta||05-14-2001||10:43 PM||||I was amazing my co-workers today with little known "facts" about the Fiero.  It is not that tough because most people don't know that much about the Fiero (as much as we do anyway).  And that got me thinking, how about some fun.  Everyone post a few little know facts about are favorite auto.  You know the ones you have tucked away in your head and pull out at your meetings or at a show when you need it.  I hope this is fun and that we all can share some great info with each other.  <P>Good luck<P>Rob<P>------------------<BR>qwikgta@yahoo.com<BR>88 T-Top coupe<BR>http://robsfieroproject.homestead.com/index.html<BR>http://vafiero.com||||reg||1
Z||000001||DJRice||05-14-2001||10:46 PM||||Hmm...The fiero was the first automobile to be spotted on the surface of Mars.<P>------------------<BR>Dillon<BR>Black '87 SE V6<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/djr_signature.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Bluebottlejunky||05-14-2001||11:18 PM||||Well i heard this at Michigan fiero fest 2000...anyway the first fiero off the line to be sold "white 84 SE" when they took it off the line and started to drive away, all 4 wheels went flying off..hehe something was wrong with he lug machine.  Heard that from the "father of the fiero"  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Mike<BR>85'GT 4sp, <BR>AOL IM: Fierofanatic2001||||reg||1
Z||000003||Haze_Performance||05-15-2001||12:29 AM||||1) Most people don't know that the Fiero has a courtesy light under the hood. (Front)<P>2) In 1986 there was 5 Experimental colors painted on the Fiero. (Never Released) There was 2 in 1987. (Also Never Released)<P>3) In 1988 the Fiero V6 & Firebird V6/5.0L V8 use the same Multec fuel injectors.<P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.ws6fiero.com" TARGET=_blank><BR>           <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/haze8588logo.gif">      </A>       <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/WS6_Fiero/photo.html" TARGET=_blank><BR>Pennock's Fiero Forum Members Photo Page</A><BR><I>If you want to add your Fiero to the collection, post or send me a photo. (Sent photos ONLY to: purplehazeracing@yahoo.com )</I><P><A HREF="http://www.clubs.yahoo.com/clubs/ws6fiero" TARGET=_blank>WS6 Fiero Club</A>||||reg||14
Z||000004||Black88GT||05-15-2001||01:14 AM||||1.) The '88 Fiero did feature the first automotive use of nickel coated graphic fiber (NCG) as a shield against electromagnetic and radio frequency interference (EMI and RFI). The chopped NCG fibers were supplied as a non-woven mat resembling fiberglass. The three main horizontal plastic panels (hood, front roof section, and rear deck lid) of all Fieros are made of fiberglass/polyester sheet molding compound (SMC. The 1988 Fiero added a layer of the NCG matting to the uncurred SMC for the rear deck lid only. During the molding process, the heat and pressure bonded the NCG and SMC together. No additional assembly was required.<P>2.) Referring to the Power Steering thing on '88s, some reports say the cancellation of the Fiero left no reason to spend the money to produce the steering unit, other reports blame the excessive noise made by the unit for its omission from the 1988 model.  <P><P>------------------<BR>Jeff (AOL IM - FieroTT)<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD - MAFOA<BR>          <IMG SRC="http://88database.homestead.com/files/AF.gif">     <BR><I>"Once you go black, you never go back..."</I><BR><I>"The Customer Can Have Any Color He Wants So Long As It's Black" </I> -Henry Ford||||reg||1
Z||000005||skitime||05-15-2001||07:43 AM||||The courtesy light under the hood is only on cars with sunroofs and only works with the parking lights on.||||reg||1
Z||000006||FieroJoe||05-15-2001||07:49 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by skitime:<BR><B>The courtesy light under the hood is only on cars with sunroofs and only works with the parking lights on.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Hmm, I dont have a sunroof and I have one.  It too only works with the parking lights, though my Helm manual says it is supposed to work with the hood switch.  It says nothing in there about only having it on a car with a sunroof.<BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/joesig_1.jpg"> <BR>'87 Coupe 5spd.<BR>AIM:FieroJoe87||||reg||1
Z||000007||wkayl||05-15-2001||07:49 AM||||In 1986 Coca-Cola gave away red Fiero GTs.  If you emptied a can and won $100 it put you in a pool of people who pulled a key from a fish bowl to see if it would start the car.  Here is the one we gave away...<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grandopening_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000008||skitime||05-15-2001||08:46 AM||||Maybe that is a 88 only thing because my 88 T-top does not have the courtesy light.   ||||reg||1
Z||000009||banditbalz||05-15-2001||09:27 AM||||How about this one... At 100 km/h (64 mp/h) there is an 80lb downforce on the rear wheels on Fieros equipped with factory wings.<P>Silver 86 GT<BR>completely stock,<BR>completely fast!<BR>  <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/banditbalz/" TARGET=_blank>www.geocities.com/banditbalz/</A> <BR><p>[This message has been edited by banditbalz (edited 05-15-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000010||ChadMan||05-15-2001||10:25 AM||||According to Road and Track, the "bumper pad" nose (84-86 Coupes) generates 100 lbs of lift at 100 mph.<P>So if banditbalz and I are both right, if you put a wing on an 84-86 Coupe and drive it fast enough, would it flip over backwards???||||reg||1
Z||000011||Slammed Fiero||05-15-2001||10:27 AM||||The 88 Power steering units (hydro electric) Were the prototypes for the Lotus esprit system as well. This is the only true relationship between Fiero and Lotus.<P>This from a former engineer with Lotus.<P><P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1607505&a=12259132&p=48230089&Sequence=0&res=high">     <BR>Jonathan McCreery<BR>86 GT 4spd<BR>Koni's , Coilovers, Big Bars , 17" Trmotorsports Typhoons , 11.25" vented discs, Wilwood 4 Piston Calipers , Pirelli P Zero's, Short Shift, No cat , Cold air induction , Geni Stainless tips, White face gauges , Momo shift , momo pedals..Autocrossed , Tracked , abused.||||reg||1
Z||000012||LZeitgeist||05-15-2001||12:57 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>This is the only true relationship between Fiero and Lotus.<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Not entirely true... from what I've read, one of the engineers that helped design the original Fiero suspension (the version that finally made its way underneath the '88's) at one time worked for Lotus in one capacity or another. Years went by between the two modes of employment, and he didn't bring any suspension information from Lotus that was used on the Fiero that I'm aware of. <P>It's a tenuous relationship, but it exists. ||||reg||1
Z||000013||Ken Wittlief||05-15-2001||01:26 PM||||I read in the 'Fiero' book, that engineers tried for years to get Ponitac to approve a 2 seater sports car program, and it repeatedly got shot down cause: The 4 seater T bird sold better than the 2 seater, and the Vette lost money for a long time before it finally turned any profit.<P>  Late in the 70's car producers had to meet federal mpg average ratings for all cars sold, and Pontiac was thinking of spending 250 million dollars to develop an effecient 4 speed auto transmission.<P>  Some on the engineers that had been pushing for the 2 seater came up with the idea, if we can promote this idea as a commuter car, and if we can sell 100k units a year that get 50mpg, and we can do it for 250 million of capitol investment, it would be a better way to go than developing the 4 speed auto for the bigger cars.<P>  It was pitched that way, and thanks to the threat of $5/gallon gas prices expected in the early 80s and the promise of 50mpg from the 'P-car' project (as it was called then), the Fiero program was finally approved.<P>  Funny thing is, $5/gallon never happend. Neither did 50mpg in a Fiero.||||reg||1
Z||000014||rogergarrison||05-15-2001||09:14 PM||||I dont know if this is a fact or not concerning the Corvette (from a local member of NCRS) national Corvette club. The Corvette has never been profitable to GM, they make them at a loss for image only. Just call it a big ad budget.||||reg||1
Z||000015||Slammed Fiero||05-15-2001||09:21 PM||||84 Corvette Production was nearly 1 third that of the fiero. The fiero outsold the Corvette every year , Including 1988 when they never ran a full production year.<P>The Vette has been making money since the introduction of the C5 in 97 , but it was some 20 years before they turned a profit, the Corvette program was sponsored by the CK truck Division in the dark years.<P><P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1607505&a=12259132&p=48230089&Sequence=0&res=high">     <BR>Jonathan McCreery<BR>86 GT 4spd<BR>Koni's , Coilovers, Big Bars , 17" Trmotorsports Typhoons , 11.25" vented discs, Wilwood 4 Piston Calipers , Pirelli P Zero's, Short Shift, No cat , Cold air induction , Geni Stainless tips, White face gauges , Momo shift , momo pedals..Autocrossed , Tracked , abused.||||reg||1
Z||000016||Fformula88||05-15-2001||09:23 PM||||I've been told that a number of 88 Fiero's were produced with power steering installed.  I think the number I was told was 16 or so pre-production power steering equipped Fiero's rolled out of the factory for testing.  <P>I've never seen one, or heard of anyone that has had one and don't even know if its true.<P>I'd also imagine they didn't install it because of the cancelation over the noise.  They had it advertised in their press releases and publications that it was going to be a mid-year option.  I have two Pontiac magazines that promote it!||||reg||1
Z||000017||Raydar||05-15-2001||10:00 PM||||The exploded images and part numbers for the power steering are also in the 22-P book.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 black Formula<BR>88 Duke coupe <BR>88 "wadded up" Formula (parts car)||||reg||1
Z||000018||FieroHarry||05-15-2001||11:03 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroJoe:<BR><B> <BR>Hmm, I dont have a sunroof and I have one.  It too only works with the parking lights, though my Helm manual says it is supposed to work with the hood switch.  It says nothing in there about only having it on a car with a sunroof.<P><BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>It does work only with the hood switch, if the hood isnt open the light never comes on <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR><B>Harry Waggoner</B><BR>FOCOSEVA,FOCOA<BR>1985 GT 262K+ <I>"TEMPTATION"</I>||||reg||1
Z||000019||LZeitgeist||05-15-2001||11:28 PM||||Actually, you're both right - the front compartment light only comes on when BOTH the front compartment is open AND the parking lights are on. It never comes on any other way.<P>Just an aside - my first Fiero was an '88 Coupe, no factory sunroof, no power windows/locks/anything, no courtesy light kit under the dash/in the rear trunk - but it still had the light bulb socket wired into the front compartment. It didn't have the reflector bracket, but it did have the socket hanging free, and it works just fine with a bulb installed. I would imagine that it came in every '88, if not before - it might have just not had the reflector bracket installed unless there were certain other options purchased. ||||reg||1
Z||000020||Ken Wittlief||05-15-2001||11:42 PM||||ok you guys are starting to drive me buggy with this courtisy light thing! Where exactly is it located? In the front trunk (on the lid or on the firewall somewhere)?<P>under the dash?!?! why would you want a light under the dahboard to go on when you open the front trunk with the parking lights on ?!?!?<P> I have an 85 SE and I have the light in the rear trunk that works whenever the engine lid is up, but i cant find anything up front.<P>but there is a switch on the front trunk lid, my only guess is that its for the LID open warning lite?||||reg||1
Z||000021||kslish||05-16-2001||02:39 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Fformula88:<BR><B>I've been told that a number of 88 Fiero's were produced with power steering installed.  I think the number I was told was 16 or so pre-production power steering equipped Fiero's rolled out of the factory for testing.  <P>I've never seen one, or heard of anyone that has had one and don't even know if its true.<P>I'd also imagine they didn't install it because of the cancelation over the noise.  They had it advertised in their press releases and publications that it was going to be a mid-year option.  I have two Pontiac magazines that promote it!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Actually, I remember hearing the same thing about a short run of '88GT's that were built with power steering, but GM yanked the units before they were delivered to the dealerships.  GM decided they didn't want to go through the expense of stocking replacement parts for the system since they would have been on such a small amount of Fieros as a whole (the system became ready after GM had alredy decided to cancel the Fiero at the end of the model year).  <P>Anyways, GM did eventually use the Fiero's electro-hydraulic power steering system.  It appeared on their electric car, the Saturn EV1.  This was stated in a review of the EV1 by MotorTrend.<P>Ken S.<BR>'87GT and '86SC<BR> <A HREF="http://www.westpennfiero.org" TARGET=_blank>www.westpennfiero.org</A> <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000022||mrfixit58||05-16-2001||08:07 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Fformula88:<BR><B>I've been told that a number of 88 Fiero's were produced with power steering installed.  I think the number I was told was 16 or so pre-production power steering equipped Fiero's rolled out of the factory for testing.  <P>I've never seen one, or heard of anyone that has had one and don't even know if its true.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Rodney Dickman has an actual Fiero power steering unit. I don't remember where he got it but it was not installed on a car. Right now (or, a least since the last time he mentioned it) it just -- for display purposes, only. Although, he has mentioned that he is tempted to actually install it.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Roy :D<BR>87 GT  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pennocksize.JPG"> ||||reg||7
Z||000023||Oreif||05-16-2001||09:43 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by kslish:<BR><B> <P><BR>Anyways, GM did eventually use the Fiero's electro-hydraulic power steering system.  It appeared on their electric car, the Saturn EV1.  This was stated in a review of the EV1 by MotorTrend.<P>Ken S.<BR>'87GT and '86SC<BR> <A HREF="http://www.westpennfiero.org" TARGET=_blank>www.westpennfiero.org</A> </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>So if you happen to see an EV1 in a junk yard and own an 88 Fiero, it looks like you'll be able to have power steering!?!<BR>HMM that is very instresting.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000024||Jefrysuko||05-16-2001||11:40 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by mrfixit58:<BR><B> Rodney Dickman has an actual Fiero power steering unit. I don't remember where he got it but it was not installed on a car. Right now (or, a least since the last time he mentioned it) it just -- for display purposes, only. Although, he has mentioned that he is tempted to actually install it.<P><BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The unit that Rodney has on his car came off a Zimmer.  It used a modified rack from a Mercury Mercur.  It wasn't electric either.  They zimmer somehow had a pump mounted a pump on the 2.8.  Since this was made to fit the Zimmer I don't think that Rodney had much modifications needed to make it fit.<P>Jeffrey D Suckow||||reg||1
Z||000025||LZeitgeist||05-16-2001||02:03 PM||||Ken sez:<BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>ok you guys are starting to drive me buggy with this courtisy light thing! Where exactly is it located? In the front trunk (on the lid or on the firewall somewhere)?<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>It is in the front compartment, in the wiring harness running along the 'firewall', near the centerline of the car, a bit closer to the passenger side. It is a small black socket, and it is very similar to the sockets that are used in the side marker lights, and this light uses the same bulb as the side markers do.<P><BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>under the dash?!?! why would you want a light under the dahboard to go on when you open the front trunk with the parking lights on ?!?!?<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I can't tell if you're being funny or not, so I'll answer it seriously. The lights under the dash to which I refer are part of an option package that included courtesy lights under the dash that came on with the overhead dome/courtesy light as well as the light that comes on in the rear trunk compartment. I mentioned this to point out that the front compartment light socket is still included on cars that lack the extra courtesy lights, even though the bracket is probably only available with the rest of the package. The socket is built into the wiring harness regardless of option package.<P>The under-dash lights have nothing to do with whether or not the front hood is open.<P><BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>I have an 85 SE and I have the light in the rear trunk that works whenever the engine lid is up, but i cant find anything up front.<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Take a closer look in the areas I mentioned above. It *may* not be in every model - however, the light has been found in all three '88's I have had access to, as well as an '87 GT my father and I parted out.<P><BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>but there is a switch on the front trunk lid, my only guess is that its for the LID open warning lite?<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>If you are speaking of the white-topped pushbutton at the base of the windshield, yes, this is the switch that turns on the "Ajar" light in the instrument cluster when the front hood is opened.<P>Hope this helps...<BR>||||reg||1
